{"v":1,"by":"the-game-bureau","isNew":false,"at":1795829410013,"game":{"kit":"notebook","layout":"product","slug":"wordfleet2","title":"WORD FLEET","kicker":"The Game Bureau presents","brand":{"color":"#2A6130","accent":"#FF9F40","paper":"#F1F3EE","ink":"#1B231F"},"tagline":"Battleship Meets Wordle","shareText":"WORD FLEET: One sentence that says what the game is and why it's fun.","announce":"","price":"$9.99","currency":"USD","order":{"url":"","label":"ORDER PRINTED NOTEBOOK","shippingNote":"Shipping calculated at checkout."},"media":[{"type":"image","src":"images/wfbg.jpg","alt":""},{"type":"image","src":"images/battle-sheet-preview.jpg","alt":""},{"type":"video","src":"/studio/assets/notebook-open.mp4","alt":"Placeholder video","placeholder":true}],"aboutHeading":"What it is","description":["Open the Word Fleet Game Notebook, grab a pencil, and challenge a friend to a duel of hidden words. Each battle sheet gives you one grid to hide your word-ships and another to track your shots, guesses, and clues."],"specs":[["CAPTAINS","2"],["TIME","About 10 minutes"],["AGES","9+"]],"stepsHeading":"How it works","steps":[{"title":"PLOT YOUR FLEET","text":"Each captain tears a Battle Tracker out of the notebook and keeps the printed words hidden from their opponent. Place your five words of 5, 4, 3, 3, and 2 letters on your Defense Grid, across or down, one letter per square."},{"title":"Play","text":"Start your attack by guessing one whole enemy word-ship. A correct guess lets you call a coordinate and take a shot. A wrong guess ends your turn. If your shot hits, take one guess at the letter in that square."},{"title":"DEMAND SURRENDER","text":"When you think you’ve found the entire fleet, name all five words and their exact locations. Get them all right and you win. One wrong word or location costs you the game."}],"videoHeading":"See it played","rulesBlurb":"Everything you need to play, on one page. The same rules are printed inside the notebook.","setup":{},"print":{"trim":[8.5,11],"bleed":0.125,"margin":0.5,"spinePerPage":0.002252,"padTo":2,"sheets":72,"author":"The Game Bureau"},"subtitle":"SINK OR SPELL","rulesName":"Rules OF ENGAGEMENT","pages":{"source":"generator","generator":"wordfleet-battle-sheets","edition":"wordfleet2/pages/20261127-1259.json"}},"rules":"<h1>Rules of Engagement</h1>\n\n<p class=\"rule-specs\">2 captains &middot; 15&ndash;30 minutes &middot; Ages 10+</p>\n\n<p>Hide a fleet of five words on your battle sheet. Guess a whole enemy word-ship to earn a shot. Win by naming every word in the opposing fleet and exactly where it is hidden.</p>\n\n<nav class=\"rule-contents\">\n<h2>In this guide</h2>\n<ol>\n  <li><a href=\"#battle-sheets\">Get your battle sheets ready</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#deploy\">Deploy your word-ships</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#first-shot\">Decide who goes first</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#turns\">Take a turn</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#surrender\">Demand surrender</a></li>\n</ol>\n</nav>\n\n<h2 id=\"battle-sheets\">Get your battle sheets ready</h2>\n\n<p>Each captain tears a <strong>Battle Tracker</strong> out of the notebook or takes a printed sheet. Keep your words and launch codes hidden from your opponent. Grab a pencil and fill in the <strong>Fleet Name</strong> line.</p>\n\n<div class=\"rule-side\">\n<dl>\n  <dt>Attack Grid</dt>\n  <dd>Track your shots and the letters you uncover in your opponent’s fleet.</dd>\n  <dt>Attack Manifest</dt>\n  <dd>Use these alphabet boxes to keep track of the letter tallies your opponent gives you.</dd>\n  <dt>Defense Grid</dt>\n  <dd>Hide your own word-ships here.</dd>\n  <dt>Defense Manifest</dt>\n  <dd>Look here to see how many times each letter appears in your own fleet.</dd>\n  <dt>Launch Codes</dt>\n  <dd>Use these five secret numbers to bluff for the first turn.</dd>\n</dl>\n<figure class=\"rule-pic\">\n  <a href=\"rules/battle-sheet-preview.webp\"><img src=\"rules/battle-sheet-preview.webp\" width=\"918\" height=\"1188\" alt=\"Open a full-size sample battle sheet\"></a>\n  <figcaption>Sample battle sheet</figcaption>\n</figure>\n</div>\n\n<h2 id=\"deploy\">Deploy your word-ships</h2>\n\n<p>Find the five words printed above your Defense Grid. They are <strong>5, 4, 3, 3, and 2 letters</strong> long. Each word is one ship.</p>\n\n<ol>\n  <li>Pick a starting square for each word and write one letter per square.</li>\n  <li>Place the letters left to right across a row or top to bottom down a column.</li>\n  <li>Give each ship its own squares inside the grid. Ships may touch.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<aside class=\"callout\"><p><strong>Example.</strong> Place MAP across C4, D4, and E4. Write M in C4, A in D4, and P in E4.</p></aside>\n\n<h2 id=\"first-shot\">Decide who goes first</h2>\n\n<p>Either captain calls out a three-digit launch code from <strong>000 to 999</strong>. It can be a code printed on their sheet or a bluff. The other captain chooses one response.</p>\n\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr><th scope=\"col\">Response</th><th scope=\"col\">What happens</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><th scope=\"row\">Concede</th><td>The captain who called the code takes the first turn.</td></tr>\n    <tr><th scope=\"row\">Challenge</th><td>The caller must prove the code appears on their sheet. If it does, the caller goes first. If it was a bluff, the challenger goes first.</td></tr>\n    <tr><th scope=\"row\">Counter</th><td>Call an equal or higher code. You become the new caller and the other captain now chooses a response.</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>Keep going until someone concedes or a challenge settles who goes first.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"callout\"><p><strong>Example.</strong> You call 850. Your opponent counters with 900. You challenge, and 900 is missing from their sheet. You take the first turn.</p></aside>\n\n<h2 id=\"turns\">Take a turn</h2>\n\n<p>Alternate turns. At the start of your turn, choose a standard attack or <a href=\"#surrender\">demand surrender</a>.</p>\n\n<h3>Guess a whole word-ship before you fire</h3>\n\n<p>Say one complete word you think is in your opponent’s fleet. Your opponent checks their word list.</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Correct word.</strong> You earn a shot. Call a coordinate to fire.</li>\n  <li><strong>Wrong word.</strong> Your turn ends immediately. Pass play to the other captain.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Call a coordinate</h3>\n\n<p>Call a column letter from A to J and a row number from 1 to 10, such as <strong>E7</strong>. Your opponent checks that square on their Defense Grid and calls a hit or a miss.</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Miss.</strong> Put a dot in that square on your Attack Grid and pass the turn.</li>\n  <li><strong>Hit.</strong> Outline the square on your Attack Grid. Take one guess at the letter in that square.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Guess one letter after a hit</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Correct letter.</strong> Your opponent confirms it. Write the letter in the square and pass the turn.</li>\n  <li><strong>Wrong letter.</strong> Your opponent checks their Defense Manifest and tells you how many times the letter you guessed appears across their entire fleet, including letters already found. Record the tally and pass the turn.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>You can fire at a square you hit before on a later turn to try a different letter.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"callout\"><p><strong>Example.</strong> You correctly guess TIDE and earn a shot. You hit E4 and guess A. The square holds P, and A appears twice in the opposing fleet. Your opponent says “A tally 2.” Mark the hit, record the tally, and pass the turn.</p></aside>\n\n<h2 id=\"surrender\">Demand surrender</h2>\n\n<p>At the start of your turn, you can demand surrender in place of attacking. Say all five enemy words, their spellings, and the first and last coordinates of each word.</p>\n\n<p>Your opponent waits for you to finish calling the whole fleet, then checks every word and location against their Defense Grid.</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Everything is right.</strong> You win immediately.</li>\n  <li><strong>Any word, spelling, or location is wrong.</strong> Your opponent wins immediately.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<aside class=\"callout\"><p><strong>Example.</strong> Call “MAP, M-A-P, from C4 to E4,” then give the same information for the other four word-ships.</p></aside>\n","cover":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex\">\n<title>Cover</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/studio/kit/print.css?v=c84c3880b4\">\n<script src=\"/studio/kit/kit.js?v=c84c3880b4\"></script>\n<script src=\"/studio/kit/print.js?v=c84c3880b4\"></script>\n<!--\n  COVER (Split style, from the studio's cover styles). Design the front and the back here; print.js places them:\n    ?layout=spread  back | spine | front, with bleed (the printer's cover PDF)\n    ?layout=front   front alone at trim size (first page of the print-at-home and sampler PDFs; the sampler adds its stamp on top)\n    ?layout=back    back alone at trim size (last page of those PDFs)\n  .cover-front and .cover-back fill their panel to the bleed edge, with padding set for you so\n  words stay in the safe area. Pictures may run to the bleed; words never leave the padding.\n  Filled from game.json: {{title}} {{subtitle}} {{tagline}} {{kicker}} {{url}} {{price}},\n  and as HTML: {{steps}} {{specs}} {{description}} {{image}} {{qr}} {{stepsHeading}}\n  ({{image}} is the photo marked FOR NOTEBOOK COVER in Media, or a pattern of squares when none is).\n  Colours: var(--brand) var(--accent) var(--paper) var(--ink), plus var(--on-brand) and var(--on-accent)\n  (white or ink, whichever reads on that colour) and var(--brand-ink) (the main colour, or ink when it is too pale on paper).\n  Type on every style: kicker 10pt Text caps, title in Display caps, subtitle 24pt Display caps, web address 9pt.\n-->\n<style>\n/* Front: the photo across the top 58% to the bleed, an accent rule, then the words on the main colour below. */\n.cover-front .kick{font:800 10pt/1.2 \"NB Text\",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase}\n.cover-front h1{line-height:.9;text-transform:uppercase;text-wrap:balance;overflow-wrap:break-word}\n.cover-front .sub{font:400 24pt/1.05 \"NB Display\",Impact,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;text-wrap:balance}\n.cover-front .kick:empty,.cover-front .sub:empty{display:none}\n.cover-front .pk-url{font:700 9pt/1.2 \"NB Text\",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-top:auto;padding-top:12pt;opacity:.85}\n.cover-front{background:var(--brand);color:var(--on-brand);justify-content:flex-end;overflow:hidden}\n.cover-front .pic{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:0;height:58%;overflow:hidden;border-bottom:10pt solid var(--accent);display:grid;place-items:center;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--brand) 80%,#000)}\n.cover-front .pic .pk-image{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;max-height:none;margin:0;border-radius:0;object-fit:cover}\n.cover-front>:not(.pic){position:relative}\n.cover-front .kick{color:var(--accent)}\n.cover-front h1{font-size:88pt;margin-top:10pt;max-width:7.5in}\n.cover-front .sub{margin-top:12pt}\n.cover-front .pk-url{margin-top:0;padding-top:.3in}\n\n/* BACK: \"Poster\". The main colour to the bleed, photo 1 echoed faintly behind so the wrap\n   reads as one piece, then, sitting at the bottom just above the footer, the kicker, the title, the hook in the accent\n   colour and the tagline, and a footer band with a QR code to the game page, \"Scan for updates and other game notebooks\" and the address. */\n.cover-back{background:var(--brand);color:var(--on-brand);overflow:hidden;gap:0}\n.cover-back .bk-echo{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:0;bottom:0;overflow:hidden;z-index:0}\n.cover-back .bk-echo .pk-image{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;max-height:none;margin:0;border-radius:0;object-fit:cover;filter:grayscale(1) contrast(1.15);mix-blend-mode:luminosity;opacity:.28}\n.cover-back .bk-echo .pk-art{display:none}\n.cover-back .bk-echo::after{content:\"\";position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(to bottom,color-mix(in srgb,var(--brand) 20%,transparent) 30%,var(--brand) 92%)}\n.cover-back>*:not(.bk-echo){position:relative;z-index:1}\n.cover-back .bk-kick{margin-top:auto;font:800 10pt/1.2 \"NB Text\",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--on-brand) 80%,transparent)}\n.cover-back .bk-kick:empty{display:none}\n.cover-back .bk-title{font:400 92pt/.9 \"NB Display\",Impact,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.01em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:10pt;max-width:7in;text-wrap:balance}\n.cover-back h2{font-size:40pt;line-height:.95;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);margin-top:14pt;max-width:6.6in;text-wrap:balance}\n.cover-back h2:empty{display:none}\n.cover-back .bk-tag{font:500 15pt/1.4 \"NB Text\",sans-serif;margin:16pt 0 0;max-width:6in}\n.cover-back .bk-tag:empty{display:none}\n.cover-back .bk-foot{margin:.4in calc(-1 * var(--pad)) calc(-1 * var(--pad));padding:.22in var(--pad) var(--pad);background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:14pt}\n.cover-back .pk-qr{width:1.05in;height:1.05in;color:var(--ink);flex:none}\n.cover-back .bk-scan{font:400 10pt/1.35 \"NB Text\",sans-serif;flex:1;align-self:center}\n.cover-back .bk-scan b{display:block;font:400 17pt/1 \"NB Display\",Impact,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.03em;color:var(--brand-ink);margin-bottom:4pt;text-transform:uppercase}\n.cover-back .bk-url{display:block;font:800 12pt/1.2 \"NB Text\",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.02em}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body data-page=\"cover\">\n\n<div class=\"cover-front\">\n  <div class=\"pic\">{{image}}</div>\n  <div class=\"kick\">{{kicker}}</div>\n  <h1>{{title}}</h1>\n  <div class=\"sub\">{{subtitle}}</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"cover-spine\">{{title}}</div>\n\n<div class=\"cover-back\">\n  <div class=\"bk-echo\">{{image}}</div>\n  <div class=\"bk-kick\">{{kicker}}</div>\n  <div class=\"bk-title\">{{title}}</div>\n  <h2>{{subtitle}}</h2>\n  <p class=\"bk-tag\">{{tagline}}</p>\n  <div class=\"bk-foot\">\n    {{qr}}\n    <div class=\"bk-scan\"><b>Scan for updates and other game notebooks</b><span class=\"bk-url\">{{url}}</span></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n","contents":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex\">\n<title>Contents</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/studio/kit/print.css\">\n<script src=\"/studio/kit/kit.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"/studio/kit/print.js\"></script>\n<!--\n  CONTENTS: every inside page of the notebook, in order.\n  - <section data-rules> is replaced by rules.md and flows onto as many pages as it needs.\n  - Each <section class=\"page\"> is one fixed page; its padding keeps content in the safe area.\n  - <template data-repeat=\"N\" data-per=\"2\"> repeats its pages N times. Inside it, {{n}} numbers\n    the copies (1, 2, 3...) and {{i}} {{i+1}} number the items on each copy (1-2, 3-4...).\n    {{sheets}} is print.sheets in game.json (set on the admin page).\n  - Filled from game.json: {{title}} {{subtitle}} {{tagline}} {{url}} {{price}} {{sheets}}.\n-->\n<style>\n.page h2{font-size:28pt;color:var(--brand)}\n.page .lede{margin:4pt 0 12pt;font-size:10pt}\n.grid{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed}\n.grid th,.grid td{border:1pt solid var(--ink);height:.3in;font-size:9pt;text-align:center}\n.grid thead th{background:var(--brand);color:#fff;font:400 11pt \"NB Display\",Impact,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;height:.42in}\n.grid th.r{width:.7in;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 25%,#fff);color:var(--ink);font:400 11pt \"NB Display\",Impact,sans-serif}\n.grid tfoot th,.grid tfoot td{height:.42in;border-width:2pt}\n\n.sheet{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10pt}\n.sheet-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;border-bottom:2pt solid var(--ink);padding-bottom:4pt}\n.sheet-head .fill{display:flex;gap:16pt;font:800 8pt \"NB Text\",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em}\n.sheet-head .fill span{border-bottom:1pt solid var(--ink);min-width:1.3in}\n.notes{flex:1;border:1pt solid var(--ink);border-radius:4pt;padding:8pt;font:800 8pt \"NB Text\",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;\n  background:repeating-linear-gradient(transparent 0 .3in,color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 25%,transparent) .3in calc(.3in + .6pt))}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body data-page=\"contents\">\n\n<section data-rules></section>\n\n<section class=\"page\">\n  <h2>{{title}} Score Book</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Write each player's name at the top of a column. Record every game in its row.</p>\n  <table class=\"grid\">\n    <thead><tr><th class=\"r\">GAME</th><th>PLAYER 1</th><th>PLAYER 2</th><th>PLAYER 3</th><th>PLAYER 4</th><th>PLAYER 5</th><th>PLAYER 6</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody id=\"score-rows\"></tbody>\n    <tfoot><tr><th class=\"r\">TOTAL</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tfoot>\n  </table>\n</section>\n\n<template data-repeat=\"{{sheets}}\">\n  <section class=\"page sheet\">\n    <div class=\"sheet-head\"><h2>{{title}} · GAME {{n}}</h2><div class=\"fill\"><span>DATE</span><span>WINNER</span></div></div>\n    <table class=\"grid\">\n      <thead><tr><th class=\"r\">ROUND</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">1</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">2</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">3</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">4</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">5</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">6</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">7</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">8</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n      <tfoot><tr><th class=\"r\">TOTAL</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tfoot>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"notes\">NOTES</div>\n  </section>\n</template>\n\n<script>\n// Score Book rows: one per game sheet.\n(function () {\n  const n = 24;\n  let rows = '';\n  for (let r = 1; r <= n; r++) rows += '<tr><th class=\"r\">' + r + '</th>' + '<td></td>'.repeat(6) + '</tr>';\n  document.getElementById('score-rows').innerHTML = rows;\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","sampler":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"noindex\">\n<title>Sampler</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/studio/kit/print.css\">\n<script src=\"/studio/kit/kit.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"/studio/kit/print.js\"></script>\n<!--\n  SAMPLER: the free sampler's own pages, in order. The free sampler PDF is always: the chosen\n  front cover with the SAMPLER stamp, the rules, the scoring pages from contents.html, then these\n  pages. Nothing else. So the rules and scoring pages are not repeated here. Separate from contents.html.\n  - Each <section class=\"page\"> is one fixed page; its padding keeps content in the safe area.\n  - <template data-repeat=\"N\" data-per=\"2\"> repeats its pages N times. Inside it, {{n}} numbers\n    the copies (1, 2, 3...) and {{i}} {{i+1}} number the items on each copy (1-2, 3-4...).\n    {{sheets}} is print.sheets in game.json (set on the admin page).\n  - Filled from game.json: {{title}} {{subtitle}} {{tagline}} {{url}} {{price}} {{sheets}}.\n-->\n<style>\n.page h2{font-size:28pt;color:var(--brand)}\n.page .lede{margin:4pt 0 12pt;font-size:10pt}\n.grid{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed}\n.grid th,.grid td{border:1pt solid var(--ink);height:.3in;font-size:9pt;text-align:center}\n.grid thead th{background:var(--brand);color:#fff;font:400 11pt \"NB Display\",Impact,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;height:.42in}\n.grid th.r{width:.7in;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent) 25%,#fff);color:var(--ink);font:400 11pt \"NB Display\",Impact,sans-serif}\n.grid tfoot th,.grid tfoot td{height:.42in;border-width:2pt}\n\n.sheet{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10pt}\n.sheet-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;border-bottom:2pt solid var(--ink);padding-bottom:4pt}\n.sheet-head .fill{display:flex;gap:16pt;font:800 8pt \"NB Text\",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em}\n.sheet-head .fill span{border-bottom:1pt solid var(--ink);min-width:1.3in}\n.notes{flex:1;border:1pt solid var(--ink);border-radius:4pt;padding:8pt;font:800 8pt \"NB Text\",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;\n  background:repeating-linear-gradient(transparent 0 .3in,color-mix(in srgb,var(--ink) 25%,transparent) .3in calc(.3in + .6pt))}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body data-page=\"contents\">\n\n<template data-repeat=\"1\">\n  <section class=\"page sheet\">\n    <div class=\"sheet-head\"><h2>{{title}} · GAME {{n}}</h2><div class=\"fill\"><span>DATE</span><span>WINNER</span></div></div>\n    <table class=\"grid\">\n      <thead><tr><th class=\"r\">ROUND</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">1</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">2</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">3</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">4</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">5</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">6</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">7</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n        <tr><th class=\"r\">8</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n      <tfoot><tr><th class=\"r\">TOTAL</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tfoot>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"notes\">NOTES</div>\n  </section>\n</template>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n","files":{}}